Amidst the voices of shock and confusion rising up at the black smoke, Crusch’s voice informed them so as she ran over. However, though he was not suspicious of Crusch, if this was the work of Black Dog, his apprehension would win out.

Ferris: [It’s alright, I think. If not, me and Subaru-kun would end up being left behind here again, right?]

Subaru: [You’re right about that! Got it. Then right now, from here―― Invisible Providence!]

That moment, as Subaru nodded in agreement to Ferris’s comment, an invisible black magic hand emerged from his chest, and driving through the black smoke, it slammed into the face of the Knight squadron’s commanding officer, who had been attempting to charge toward them.

The commanding officer’s nose erupted with blood as he exclaimed “Kah!”, falling over on his back. Glancing at that, Crusch,

Crusch: [That person was fine.]

Subaru: [You’re kidding!? He wasn’t someone who’s been replaced!?]

Crusch: [I sensed he harbored a strong ire and hatred toward you. ]

Ferris: [It’s Knight Zeolle, right? He was in the castle at the time of the Royal Selection. Isn’t that why?]

Subaru: [Enough, please just settle on a single rating for that episode already!]

Whether it served as proof of Subaru’s innocence, or as the reason for him being targeted, the ratings were all over the place.

Setting aside that lamentation of his, disappearing into the black smoke screen, Subaru and the gang escaped the situation. ――Behind them, several members of the company of Knights attempted to follow after, but,

Kadomon: [I won’t let you chase after the kiddo and the rest. After all, I don’t like the way you Knights have conducted yourselves today one bit.]

Standing in the way to obstruct their path, was Kadomon and the gate guards.

At that unexpected assist, Subaru called out “Unc!?” in surprise, to which Kadomon smiled,

Kadomon: [Go on then, kiddo, I’ll be cheering for you! You, and Emilia-sama both!]

Subaru: [――Hk! Ahh, I’ll be coming back to collect your honest vote!]

Hearing that encouragement from Kadomon, who had acknowledged Natsuki Subaru as Emilia’s Knight, Subaru responded while on the verge of tears, and exerted strength in his legs to cross into the black smoke once more.

As he went off, the angered bellows of the squadron of Knights, and the ardor of the gate guardians defying them all flared up in a large uproar――,

Elderly Guard: [――Inspection’s finished! Let ‘em pass, you Knights! And let us guards do our jobs!!]

△▼△▼△▼△

???: [――Yo, so you’re back? I thought you’d die for sure.]

Subaru: [Chin, man, to think you were such a useless guy to have as an ally…]

After Subaru and co made it out of the enshrouding black smoke which had permitted their escape, Rachins had been waving at them as they rushed to board the dragon carriage waiting outside the gate, welcoming the four of them.

With there having been such an uproar, Subaru was shocked at Rachins’s apparent heartlessness, as he had not shown any willingness to take action.

Subaru: [Do you not have a human heart? Are you a Witch Cultist?]

Rachins: [Don’t fucking cast suspicions on people like that! Saying I didn’t do anything’s also a false accusation! I handled all the negotiations for you. Ain’t that right, Duchess-san?]

Rachins stuck out his tongue, and cued Crusch to weigh in. At that addressment, Crusch, her eyepatch reaffixed over her left eye, nodded a “That is correct”,

Crusch: [Rachins Hoffman does have a way with words. In fact, it was he who enabled negotiations to take place.]

Subaru: [Negotiations? That’d be…]

???: [――Of course, that would be with us, Natsuki-dono.]

At the voice that felt somewhat like a surprise attack, Subaru and Beatrice’s shoulders jumped with a “Pyo”.

The proprietor of the voice was none other than Russell, who had entered the dragon carriage a bit later than Subaru and the rest.

Accompanied by White Sheep and Black Dog, he shut the door to the dragon carriage, and signaled to the coachman to depart.

Instantly, the dragon carriage began to move, transforming it into an inescapable post-mortem meeting room.

Russell: [First of all, the fact that everyone returned safely is the most optimal outcome for our course of action. Of course, it was merely the result of having been blessed with good fortune, and I harbor many reservations, but―― Blue Snake.]

Ferris: [Mm…]

Russell: [You were the one to append the condition of keeping your presence among us hidden. If you take such actions regardless of that, it becomes impossible to keep it a secret. You shall not proclaim it a fault on our part, correct?]

Ferris: [I understand. I won’t call it a breach of our conditions. This isn’t the place for me to speak on my personal interests either.]

Being the first one to whom Russell had spoken out, Ferris glanced toward Crusch from the corner of his eye. However, even though Crusch had likely noticed his gaze, she gave no reaction in Ferris’s direction.

The atmosphere adrift between the two them was something extremely complex, and so――,

Subaru: [What should we do, Beako. Might I be able to do a good job of churning the atmosphere, I wonder? Should I give it a try?]

Beatrice: [For now, for now you should hold off, in fact. This is a scene for us to sit back and “observe”, I suppose. More importantly…]

Russell: [Natsuki-dono, from hereon, please refrain from taking such actions.]

Subaru: [Guh… I guess, you’re mad at me, right?]

He cautiously examined Russell’s expression, but, perhaps to be expected, the head of an intelligence agency was unreadable.

Russell’s expression was a calm sea of emotion, but there was no way that he was not angry with Subaru, who had directly disobeyed his orders, and rushed onto the scene. ――This face, was something he ought to count as indignation.

Russell: [I am not mad, just disappointed. After all, I believe I had thoroughly instilled exactly what ought to be prioritized. ――If not for Crusch-sama’s comments, I would not have risked remaining in that place.]

Subaru: [Crusch-san’s, words? Those would be…]

Crusch: [It is nothing extraordinary. ――As the situation stands, I have no intention of placing my trust in anybody here other than Natsuki Subaru. Without you here, I would refuse to cooperate with the likes of the Six Tonuges.]

Subaru: [That’s…! That’s an extreme honor, but…!]

Depending on how it was interpreted, that assessment could be a rather extreme one, and thus, Subaru fervently took mind of the surrounding gazes―― in particular, that of Russell, who’d had an unnecessary condition levied upon him, and Ferris, who bore quite a complex relationship. But then again, Russell’s expression remained unchanged, and Ferris, due to exhaustion, remained seated while averting his face.

Regardless, the Six Tongues could not afford to relinquish Crusch, so it was due to her opinion that they had been unable to abandon Subaru, Beatrice, and Ferris after they had gone back to the crash site.

Subaru: [But, this would mean, Russell-san…]

Russell: [What is it? If your mind has changed over the course of this incident…]

Subaru: [Rather than my mind per-se, this is just a hypothetical, but if something like this were to happen again, I think Ferris and I probably wouldn’t be able to leave it alone. Hence, I have a request.]

Russell: [――. Let us hear it.]

Subaru: [From here on out, I’d like to go with strategies that, well, cause as little harm to others as possible. ――Is that no good?]

Russell slightly widened his eyes at that plea, and behind him, Black Dog laughed a “Kuha”.

He was aware that he was saying something unreasonable. But, as a matter of fact, nobody had died during the incident on this occasion. It would be difficult when it came to dealing with those whom Capella had gotten her hands on, but they should still be able to oppose that to the very end.

As Subaru thought so, before Russell could even say anything――,

White Sheep: [M-me too! I also think… that Subaru-san’s way of doing things, is good…]

Crusch: [There is nothing more ideal than concluding things with minimal casualties. Of course, I believe that we ought to follow a certain order of priority in order to get things done, but… lives rank quite highly in my personal order of precedence.]

White Sheep and Crusch were in agreement with Subaru’s opinion, and there was also no way that Ferris would object. Black Dog’s sneer went without saying, but surprisingly, Rachins snorted his nose but did not repudiate it.

And, as a matter of course, Subaru’s like-minded best partner was――,

Beatrice: [Of course, Betty’s view is the same as Subaru’s, in fact. After all, Subaru has always silenced everyone by recklessly doing the impossible, I suppose. This time shall be no different, in fact.]

Subaru: [You’re sorta making me sound like a terrible troublemaker, but, thank you.]

Articulating so with a smile, Subaru hugged Beatrice by his lap, and plumped himself down into his seat. He was to the left of Ferris, who had sat down before him. Then, on his other side, Crusch took her seat.

Sandwiching Subaru and Beatrice, Crusch and Ferris had aligned themselves to his sides.

Subaru: [Shit. I picked the wrong seat. Um, I guess I’ll just move…]

Ferris: [Hey, Subaru-kun. Could you pass a message to the person by your side? “That strange power might place an unexpected burden on your body, so it would be best not to overrely on it~”, kay?]

Subaru: [No, err…]

Crusch: [Natsuki Subaru, pass the following message onto the individual by your side. “It is likely that I will once more fall asleep for a short while. If you are concerned regarding my body, you are free to inspect it whilst I am slumbering”, that is all.]

Subaru: [Come on, does that really need to go through me!? Let’s all just speak honestly! Both of you seem like you can talk!]

However, neither Ferris, who rested his chin in his hands as he looked to the day after tomorrow, nor Crusch, who shut her eyes as she folded her arms, were willing to lend an ear to Subaru’s cries.

Although it was extremely reassuring and joyous that Crusch and Ferris were both part of the promising ensemble to save this Kingdom, the pattern of their relationship was not yet ready to openly express their gratitude.

Subaru: [The road ahead… the road ahead will be fraught with difficulties.]

As he slumped his shoulders, crestfallen, he placed his chin on the head of Beatrice in his lap. While Beatrice felt that weight, she began to pat Subaru’s head from below without reservation.

――The battle to save Emilia, to save his comrades carving their own path, and to save the Kingdom of Lugunica all in one go, commenced. A battle that would surely be no less rigorous than any that had come before.

Indeed, in the background of that strong resolve and determination donned by Natsuki Subaru, while gazing out at the shrinking sight of the Royal Capital,

Russell: [You hadn’t written about anything of this sort in your letters, Roswaal. Did you not provide the necessary Knightly training to ensure Emilia-sama would prevail, as per your desires…?]

Thus grumbled the man of the intelligence agency forced to deal with a responsibility outside the scope of his calculations, utterly stunned as he was.
